62134	Q0	zis75	61	0.99766964	instruments_tools	The scale of law and order positions captures the general tendency to ward off everything foreign and threatening combined with the demand for the use of state means of power. The development of the scale is based on work by Fend. The scale was developed in the Youth and Violence Project at Bielefeld University.
62134	Q0	zis343	62	0.9908215	instruments_tools	Respondents age is together with sex gender the most important socio demographic variable recorded in all surveys. Age provides information about partly biologically determined development and ageing processes and positioning in the life course. It is therefore related to a variety of socio economic characteristics but also to attitudes behaviour and in particular health. It is controlled for in practically all multivariate statistical models. In most studies the age at the time of the survey is determined using questions on the month and year of birth and published as a derived variable. Membership in a birth cohort is also derived from the year of birth. It is used to depict similar overall social living conditions and experiences that lead to the construction of generations e.g. the post war generation or the baby boomers .
62134	Q0	zis80	63	0.98868763	instruments_tools	This scale measures fear reactions that have already been generalized to a certain extent. The instrument offers the possibility of identifying a need for intervention preventively i.e. before a mental or psychosomatic illness develops. The development of the scale is based on the works of Epstein 1972 and Lazarus 1966 .
