8657	Q0	zis223	10	1.4034495	instruments_tools	Due to their importance for any society gender role attitudes have been included in surveys of special groups and the entire population for several decades. In accordance to the changed opportunity structure behavior of women changed too. The question was then whether the changed opportunity structure for women their changed behavior and the women s movement had also produced changes in attitudes. The documented items acquire gender role attitudes in three dimensions. The Consequence dimension C the Gender role ideology dimension G and the Economic consequences dimension E . The first and the second dimension include four items while the last dimension includes three.
8657	Q0	zis10	11	1.3835611	instruments_tools	The OCQ measures the affective loyalty of employees to their organisation. The OCQ is based on the conceptualisation of organisational commitment as an affective attitude.
8657	Q0	zis231	12	1.3835611	instruments_tools	The scale measures attitudes to Islam in Germany and was used in the General Population Survey of the Social Sciences ALLBUS in 2012.
8657	Q0	zis121	13	1.3723435	instruments_tools	The two items documented here are intended to measure 1 trust or mistrust in other people with three indicators each and 2 the assessment of general social morality or nature. According to the theory of the Berkeley Group strongly negative attitudes towards these questions are part of a central characteristic syndrome of an authoritarian personality for which a stable cynical moralizing and pejorative attitude towards others across situations is characteristic.
8657	Q0	zis97	14	1.3688539	instruments_tools	The items documented here were used to measure the ALLBUS 96 theme Attitudes towards ethnic groups in Germany .
8657	Q0	zis215	15	1.3162345	instruments_tools	The items documented here capture ambivalent sexist attitudes towards men from the two areas of hostility and benevolence. These two areas are further subdivided into three components paternalism maternalism gender differentiation and heterosexuality. They thus operationalize the construct of ambivalent sexism according to which sexist attitudes as positive evaluations feelings of closeness security affection security as well as negative evaluations hostility perception of dominance oppression dependence are connected and simultaneously exist side by side.
8657	Q0	zis168	16	1.313024	instruments_tools	The scale Littering Environmental Aesthetics ILU records attitudes behavioural readiness and self reported behaviours from the topic of throwing away waste outdoors.
