3332	Q0	zis137	10	1.6744115	instruments_tools	The scale comprises 23 items that serve to record self controls. The concept of self control was developed within the framework of the General Theory of Crime GTOC Gottfredson and Hirschi 1990 and control theories. The GTOC represents a utilitarian theory of action in criminology which assumes that deviant behaviour arises under consideration of costs and benefits and thus corresponds to rational action. With regard to control theories Gottfredson and Hirschi 1990 assume that a person can be attributed self control as a personality trait. It is assumed that people with a low level of self control tend to perform a variety of different forms of deviant behavior provided appropriate opportunities present themselves.
3332	Q0	zis343	11	1.6636087	instruments_tools	Respondents age is together with sex gender the most important socio demographic variable recorded in all surveys. Age provides information about partly biologically determined development and ageing processes and positioning in the life course. It is therefore related to a variety of socio economic characteristics but also to attitudes behaviour and in particular health. It is controlled for in practically all multivariate statistical models. In most studies the age at the time of the survey is determined using questions on the month and year of birth and published as a derived variable. Membership in a birth cohort is also derived from the year of birth. It is used to depict similar overall social living conditions and experiences that lead to the construction of generations e.g. the post war generation or the baby boomers .
